/**
 * The walker, Aldric (BIBLE 10.2), as the Ledger's scenes show them: young and worn by the
 * road, messy brown hair, a quilted gambeson of dull gold under a leather baldric, a road-brown
 * cloak thrown back from the shoulders, dark breeches, old boots, a plain longsword. Seen three
 * quarters, facing right, toward the King, the moon on their face. Painted at four times the
 * size and traced into clusters, like the creatures. Every pose keeps the same frame (96 by
 * 85) and the same ground row, so the walker never jumps from one pose to the next: standing
 * on guard, the four frames of a stride with the sword low in one hand, and the lunge of a
 * blow, both arms out and the blade level.
 */

